# Act One

## Storm is coming

A storm gathers over the sea. The lighthouse is *dark*.

[[Open on sound only: wind, gulls, a distant bell.]]

MARA
The fishing boats will return before midnight.

ELI
(dryly)
And our lamp is broken.

MARA
Then we fix it. My father kept this light burning for thirty years.

!@Eli takes an old key from his pocket.

ELI
(offers @Mara the key)
After you.

MARA: I knew you believed in me.

They enter the lighthouse.

## Inside the lighthouse

An old brass lamp stands beneath the great lens.

ELI
No oil. No flame.

MARA
My father said this lamp once answered a song.

ELI
(skeptically)
Of course it did.

MARA
Tonight, we need to **believe** him.

Music starts to play. @@music 1 "One Small Light"

MARA
ONE SMALL LIGHT
AGAINST THE NIGHT,
ONE BRAVE SPARK
CAN GUIDE US HOME.

ELI
IF YOUR VOICE
CAN FIND THE WAY,
YOU WILL NEVER
SING ALONE.

MARA / ELI
SHINE, SHINE,
ACROSS THE SEA.
BE THE LIGHT
~
WE NEED TO SEE.

The lamp *bursts* into flame. @@out 1

ELI
(amazed)
It worked.

A thunderclap shakes the tower.

@@music 2 "Thunderclap"

@@out 2

**Blackout.**

# Act Two

## Broken window

@@music 3 "Storm Underscore"

Wind howls through a broken window. The flame flickers.

ELI
The storm is putting it out!

!@Mara shields the lamp with her coat.

MARA
(struggling)
Close the window!

ELI
(grabs the handle)
It is stuck.

MARA
Then we pull _together_.

They force the window shut. The flame steadies. @@out 3

A ship's bell sounds in the distance.

ELI
(quietly)
They are out there.

MARA
And now they can see us.

## After the storm

The storm has passed. A fishing boat enters the harbor. @Rook and @Tam leap onto the pier.

ROOK
We saw your light from the reef. One more minute and we would have hit the rocks.

TAM
(to @Eli)
Was that you singing up there?

ELI
One lamp saved an entire crew.

MARA
Not one lamp. Two people kept it burning.

[[Cut this exchange if the reprise runs long.]]

Music starts to play. @@music 4 "One Small Light (Reprise)"

CREW
SHINE, SHINE,
ACROSS THE SEA.

MARA / ELI
YOU WERE THE LIGHT
~
WE NEEDED TO SEE.

The crew raises a cheer. @@out 4

ELI
(proudly)
We make a good team.

MARA
(smiles)
Bring oil next time.

They watch the sun rise over the harbor.

**Blackout.**
